final message:
The minimum charge is in `total` in `src/invoice.ts`. An invoice whose total is below $100.00 now bills $100.00:

```ts
const MINIMUM_CENTS = 10000;

export function total(invoice: Invoice): number {
  return Math.max(MINIMUM_CENTS, subtotal(invoice) - discount(invoice) + tax(invoice));
}
```

I applied the $100.00 floor to every currency as 10000 cents, since amounts are integer cents regardless of currency. If Finance means $100 only for USD, tell me and I'll make it per-currency.

**Tests: one fails.** `test/slow/ledger.test.ts` now gets `$47592.00` where it expects `$46992.00`. The difference is $600.00, which matches the change. The fixture `INV-2051` comes to $50.00 (2 seats × $25.00). It now bills $100.00, an extra $50.00 for each of the 12 copies in the year. The test's expected value is the old total, so it is stale and needs your update. I left the test alone as you asked.

The fast suite passed at this revision (29 of 29 affected checks, no failures). I could not run `tsc --noEmit`, because the command needed approval and I did not get it, so typecheck is unverified.

